          "refId": "A",
          "editorType": "sql",
          "rawSql": "",
          "format": 0,
          "queryType": "timeseries"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Two real laps (OpenF1), compared **by distance**, not by time.\n\n- **Gap**: going up = ${b} losing time there, going down = gaining it back.\n- **Corners** (table): time won between the straight before and the straight after.\n  *why* = what the faster driver did differently at that corner.\n- Checked against official F1 sector times (typically 0.03 s off, then corrected).\n\nData is ~4 samples/s, so braking points are \u00b115 m and the gap line\ncan swing inside slow corners. Corner totals are the reliable part."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
